{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "01", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "14", "M": "55", "S": "49"}}, "news": [{"title": "Chandigarh administration eyes CHB land to bankroll periphery expansion", "para": "Chandigarh's administration is developing a strategy to monetize land owned by the Chandigarh Housing Board located in IT Park. The generated revenue will facilitate the acquisition of about 1,750 acres from nearby villages, with an anticipated expense of Rs 14,000 crore. Some portions of land are earmarked for public facilities and infrastructure, aiming to bolster planned urban growth by capitalizing on the value of government properties.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/chandigarh-administration-eyes-chb-land-to-bankroll-periphery-expansion/134610434?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-439034/134610434.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Trichy leads in property tax collection for FY27", "para": "The Trichy corporation proudly announces a 55.4% collection of the current property tax demand for the fiscal year 2026-27. By publicly exposing the top 100 property tax defaulters online, they have successfully spurred long-time non-payers into action. Additionally, the disconnection of water and sewage services has further boosted collection rates.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/trichy-leads-in-property-tax-collection-for-fy27/134610374?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-566727/134610374.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Andhra Pradesh set to pilot 3D-printed houses under PMAY-Gramin", "para": "The Andhra Pradesh government plans to leverage 3D printing technology for the construction of housing under PMAY-G. A project to build approximately 100 homes in Burripalem village is underway, with technical support from CBRI. Eligible beneficiaries will receive financial assistance between \u20b91.70 lakh and \u20b91.80 lakh. This cutting-edge technology is designed to greatly reduce both construction time and costs, while enhancing thermal comfort in the homes created.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/andhra-pradesh-set-to-pilot-3d-printed-houses-under-pmay-gramin/134610242?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-210470/134610242.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}